# B17 Phase 0. Every image in docker-compose.yml builds with `context: .`
# (the repo root), so without this file the whole working tree is sent to
# the Docker daemon on every build. The Dockerfiles' COPY lines are
# targeted, so none of the paths below ever reached an image layer, but
# they did leave this machine's working tree as build context. Part L3
# (Build Guide): private tender data "is never included in Docker images".
# Excluding it from the build context makes that hold by construction, not
# only because of which COPY lines happen to exist today.

# Private tender data (Part L3) and its local-only evaluation config.
data_private/

# Real secrets. The containers receive env through compose, never the image.
.env

# Postgres dumps from earlier live runs.
backups/

# Gitignored third-party Claude Code skills (docs/frontend-tooling.md).
.agents/

# Plan item 27: the host's own Node installs and build output. apps/web's
# Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and then `COPY apps/web .`; without these lines a
# local build copied this machine's node_modules (Windows binaries included)
# over the image's own, and its old dist/ and test reports in beside them.
# CI's checkout has none of them when it builds, so CI was never affected.
**/node_modules/
apps/web/dist/
apps/web/test-results/
apps/web/playwright-report/
apps/landing/dist/
